## 📚 Reading Order

Read these first, for every task:

1. `docs/README.md` — Reading order and the SDD workflow
2. `docs/project-overview.md` — Goals, scope
3. `docs/technology.md` — Stack, libraries, versions

Read the rest only when the task needs it (this keeps your context small):

| When the task... | Read |
|---|---|
| creates, moves or renames files | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/structure.md` — Directory structure |
| writes or changes logic | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/coding-conventions.md` — Patterns, conventions |
| formats code or touches lint | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/coding-style.md` — Lint, format |
| is a specific recurring task | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/instructions-and-work-flows/` — Step-by-step guides |

